<title>USA: Bayou Q4 shr loss $0.01 vs profit $0.02.</title>
<headline>Bayou Q4 shr loss $0.01 vs profit $0.02.</headline>
<dateline>LAPLACE, La. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS</p>
<p>			    (In Thousands, Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>					    (Unaudited)    (Audited)</p>
<p>				   Quarter Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>					   September 30,  September 30,</p>
<p>					1996     1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net Sales		    $ 52,243  $45,012 $204,426 $185,772</p>
<p> Gross Profit		    4,057    3,569   15,973   23,614</p>
<p> Operating Income		1,700    1,792    7,932   17,302</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)	     (103)	271	315   10,337</p>
<p> EPS				 (.01)	.02	.02	.79</p>
<p> Shape Shipment Tons	 150,028  121,985  580,069  503,297</p>
<p> Billet Shipment Tons	  2,598	 83   15,638   11,072</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said fiscal 1996 results overall have reflected the start-up investment in Tennessee which began operations in July 1995, decreases in selling prices, increases in the prices of certain supply items and energy, and increases in non-production strike expenses.  If the Tennessee start-up and price increases were factored out, Bayou Steel's earnings would have been as solid as last year, the company said in its statement.</p>
